Initialize a Docker Swarm Manager Node

docker swarm init --advertise-addr 172.31.1.226 (private IP of manager node)

Note: The correct flag is --advertise-addr (not --advertise -addr). 
This command initializes the current node as the Docker Swarm manager and advertises the specified IP address to other nodes joining the swarm.
===============================================================================
buntu@manager1:~$ docker swarm init --advertise-addr 172.31.1.226
Swarm initialized: current node (z3q4gs72xicap9131t1kcd7vd) is now a manager.

To add a worker to this swarm, run the following command:

    docker swarm join --token SWMTKN-1-0sugj0c8dmye00kh8p2rlgbdc5l49sesljisccjm75h274vsb4-32o4hsactw2naac7i0edrh2t6 172.31.1.226:2377

To add a manager to this swarm, run 'docker swarm join-token manager' and follow the instructions.
